sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Moonbase exact-once approval and outcome review
  accDescr: An explicit owner task is bound to current profile and workstream versions. The server checks grants, context and capacity before creating its native session. A requested tool action requires an exact one-use owner decision and a fresh authority check before execution. Actual artifacts and receipts are returned, and acceptance rechecks current workspace and artifact bytes.
  participant Owner
  participant Workbench
  participant Server
  participant Native as Owned native session
  participant Project as Scoped workspace
  Owner->>Workbench: Explicit task<br/>and consent
  Workbench->>Server: Current profile/workstream<br/>versions
  Server->>Server: Validate grants, pins<br/>and capacity
  Server->>Native: Start owned run<br/>with bounded context
  Native->>Server: Request a bound<br/>tool action
  Server->>Workbench: Exact permission<br/>and action hash
  Owner->>Workbench: Approve once<br/>or deny
  Workbench->>Server: Bound decision<br/>and revision
  Server->>Server: Recheck current authority<br/>and action
  Server->>Project: Execute only the<br/>approved operation
  Project->>Server: Actual result and<br/>file/check receipts
  Server->>Workbench: Artifact, diff<br/>and outcome
  Owner->>Workbench: Accept exact outcome<br/>or request revision
  Workbench->>Server: Outcome decision
  Server->>Server: Recheck current<br/>artifact/workspace bytes
